  "caveats": [
    "The three-way classifier uses class-weight balancing for the 81/324/324 imbalance; balanced accuracy is the fair metric (chance = 0.333). All scores are out-of-fold under GroupKFold by participant, i.e. on unseen authors.",
    "The LLM-origin detector reaches AUC ~1.0 partly as an artifact: control texts are a COMBINED embedding of two writings while drafts and edited texts are single-text embeddings, so the detector also separates 'combined vs single'. Combined with the fact that an edited text is derived from its own draft, this inflates how LLM-like edited text looks. Read the detector as corroborating H1c (edited stays close to LLM) directionally, not as an exact residual-LLM rate; a clean test needs individually embedded control texts (re-embedding)."
